From f1076f2675a331ea864e88999f4066ad551fb628 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <alexander@auralite.local>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:24:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] X7 determinism gate: one input, eight processes, three
 builds, one root
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A gate, not a subsystem. The claim is one sentence — the same ordered input,
replayed by independent nodes, produces the same state_root, the same gas bill
and the same events — and the phase exists to make that sentence measurable
rather than asserted.

The input is a pure function of one constant. detcheck::X7_SEED seeds SplitMix64,
which draws the whole workload: 4 deploys, then 1 000 transactions mixing ABI v1
calls (kv, store, events), native transfers, ABI v3 calls whose withdrawals open a
nested frame, calls to an address with no code and calls that run out of gas. No
clock, no entropy, no iteration order anywhere in generation, so the scenario is
reproducible from a number and the fixture can pin the result of running it.

"Independent" is why the gate spawns processes. Two runs in one process share
Rust's per-process hasher seed, the allocator's history and the address layout, and
can agree while a second node disagrees. Eight x7-run processes therefore replay
the same 1 004 steps and must reproduce the root, the gas, the events chain and a
rolling digest that folds every step's class, status, gas and resulting root — so a
divergence is localised to the first differing step instead of being reported as
"the roots differ".

Three build configurations stand in for three platforms, and the report says
plainly that this is what they are: debug (overflow checks on), release (opt-level
3) and release with 16 codegen units all reproduce the same three numbers, two
processes each. Three operating systems cannot be measured from one sandbox, so
that dimension is the CI job `determinism` and stays unproven until it runs.

The gate executes the shipped kv, store, events and vault bytecode and re-verifies
their BLAKE3 on every run, so X7 also re-pins X4 and X6.

Measured: 890 commits, 60 refusals, 54 failures (19 out of gas, 35 no-code, 0
traps), gas 46 375 290, state root efca4222d37347ff. Every step is classified
committed / refused / failed and the split is kept, because two nodes that
disagreed about which transactions were accepted would produce different roots.

Gates: 11 tests in x7_determinism, 322 in the workspace, 6/6 X7 negative controls
(each reddening a named test after a green baseline), 153 in total, 4 692 vectors
across 24 fixtures, 239 external crates — X7 adds no crate and no dependency.

Fixed: the deployer constant was not a funded account (one byte, InsufficientBalance
on the fourth deploy); an argument was passed to run() of contracts that take none,
so a third of the workload never ran; the vault's withdraw was sent an address in
front of its amount, so every withdrawal refused -21; and the first negative control
was green until it removed the root from the digest fold rather than the index.
